THOUGHT: The NullAway error is because getThenRegion() has a non-null return type but returns a @Nullable field. The pattern in this class is to lazily initialize nullable regions (see getElseRegion()). To fix the error without changing public API contracts elsewhere, I should mirror getElseRegion(): ensure thenRegion is initialized if null and then return it. This preserves non-null return while keeping the field nullable and avoids new errors.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/jadx && sed -i '30,36c\	public IContainer getThenRegion() {
		if (thenRegion == null) {
			thenRegion = new Region(this);
		}
		return thenRegion;
	}

	public void setThenRegion(IContainer thenRegion) {
		this.thenRegion = thenRegion;
	}' jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/dex/regions/conditions/IfRegion.java
```

